ion_probe_support.py; scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py remains the thin CLI/reporting layer. Both remain stdlib-only and independently import-safe. File impact was updated before creating the support module; a fresh plan review will be required because material changed.","timestamp":1787529371831604001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed reusable duration probe: Gerrit 2164 patchset 2 merged normally as 86c0694dd8fe after LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, and zero unresolved comments. Validation included 17 focused synthetic tests, full lint/typecheck/import-walk gates, and a frozen live-probe rerun with unchanged percentiles. The merged implementation remains read-only and does not update duration guidance.","timestamp":1787538108571705001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Close precheck found the prior plan attestation stale-code after the reviewed paths landed on main. All 11 acceptance boxes are now checked from recorded validation evidence. Re-running plan review normally against merged commit 86c0694dd8fe before retrying close; no gate bypass is being used.","timestamp":1787538263291861001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Post-merge review evidence: the normal review from the broad-fetch checkout made zero LLM calls and failed after 512.139s because `git fetch origin` hit the 300s timeout. The reusable probe correctly classified that row as unmatched/no-sidecar rather than treating it as a model-backed review. A normal retry from a main-only checkout completed with signed PASS at 813baac9b015: 28 LLM calls, deterministic 5.870s, LLM 109.148s, internal total 133.411s. The discriminating configuration difference is origin.fetch: the failing partial/promisor checkout fetches all origin heads and `resolve_ref(..., blobless=False)` invokes `git fetch --quiet --no-filter origin`, while the main-only checkout passed that boundary. This is evidence for a separate broad-fetch performance bug, not a duration attribution in the probe.","timestamp":1787542023674332001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787526911721222001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"ca8357fc-78f6-44e8-b22c-ede42b438170","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"4000-2df3-398d-44e2"},{"link_uuid":"00af4396-d3b8-438b-8544-88bb5f729499","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"d891-54f4-96c5-4b74"},{"link_uuid":"dc1003cb-b0ab-41e8-ad92-69f684ad9599","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8e17-ee21-7794-48c6"},{"link_uuid":"aef159de-ce40-4615-8437-ef16fdd94e04","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"36b1-6234-49d1-41e8"},{"link_uuid":"4f081b1a-83a5-46f7-9620-e2bd62c0ecd6","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"c6bd-b10e-74f1-407f"}],"description":"## Context\nThe duration investigation reconstructed end-to-end `review-plan` and gated-close wall time from Codex rollout logs a...\n## CLI contract and frozen example\nRepository-neutral defaults are explicit:\n- Repeatable `--log-root PATH` defaults to `~/.codex/sessions` and `~/.codex/archived_sessions`, resolved with `Path....\n- `--tracker PATH` defaults to `.tickets-tracker` relative to the invocation working directory.\n- `--since` and `--until` are optional ISO-8601 bounds; omission means unbounded on that side.\n- `--provider-prefix` is optional; omission accepts any actual provider while still requiring positive `metrics.llm_c...\n- `--current-since` is optional; omission suppresses the current-regime sensitivity. The single term `current regime`...\nThe frozen analysis is reproduced with: `python scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py summary --tracker .tickets-tracker --...\n## Plan\n- Keep `scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py` as the read-only, standard-library-only CLI/reporting layer. Extract rollout...\n- Preserve the existing modes (`summary`, `table`, `clean`, `all`, and `unmatched`) while applying the CLI contract a...\n- Add a gated-close phase breakdown. Read `COMPLETION_VERDICT`, closing `STATUS`, and completion `SIGNATURE` timestam...\n- Label every phase as direct metric, direct event interval, or inferred residual; do not imply an uninstrumented bou...\n- Add focused synthetic tests for command classification, terminal reconstruction, percentile calculation, cohort fil...\n- Run `python scripts/check_import_walk.py` in addition to focused pytest and Ruff checks. If a non-stdlib optional d...\n- Do not change agent-duration guidance in this ticket.\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] The reusable probe is stored at `scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py`.\n- [x] Source contains no literal machine-specific user-home or worktree path.\n- [x] The documented command reproduces the frozen provider-clean window.\n- [x] `--current-since 2026-08-22T00:00:00Z` selects the frozen current-regime cohort.\n- [x] No-LLM operations remain distinguishable from completed model-backed cohorts.\n- [x] Forced, status/check/help, unmatched, and interrupted operations remain distinguishable from completed model-ba...\n- [x] Gated-close output reports pre-verifier residual, deterministic verifier, LLM verifier, verdict-to-status, stat...\n- [x] Each gated-close phase is labeled as a direct metric, direct event interval, or inferred residual.\n- [x] Focused tests use synthetic fixtures only and pass.\n- [x] The standalone script passes the import-walk check without import-time side effects.\n- [x] Repository guidance remains unchanged pending separate operator confirmation.\n[full output: \"$HOME/Library/Application Support/rtk/tee/1787538198_jq_-r__description.log\"]","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py","reason":"Provide the read-only CLI and human-readable gate-duration reports."},{"path":"scripts/rebar_duration_probe_support.py","reason":"Keep rollout/tracker parsing and statistical helpers below the project module-size cap along an existing call-graph seam."},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_rebar_duration_probe.py","reason":"Exercise parsing, reconstruction, filtering, and close-phase decomposition with synthetic fixtures."}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["relates_to","36b1-6234-49d1-41e8"],["relates_to","8e17-ee21-7794-48c6"],["relates_to","c6bd-b10e-74f1-407f"],["relates_to","d891-54f4-96c5-4b74"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"0e169cff-15a2-43f7-b968-71285eee8729","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["metrics","tooling","agent-telemetry"],"ticket_id":"2bcd-4c47-6f05-4605","ticket_type":"task","title":"Persist reusable gate-duration probe","verify_commands":[{"command":"pytest -q tests/scripts/test_rebar_duration_probe.py","dd_id":"D1","dd_text":"Synthetic fixtures verify parsing, filtering, terminal reconstruction, and phase decomposition"},{"command":"ruff check scripts/rebar_duration_probe.py scripts/rebar_duration_probe_support.py tests/scripts/test_rebar_duration_probe.py","dd_id":"D2","dd_text":"The CLI, support module, and focused tests satisfy repository lint rules"},{"command":"python scripts/check_import_walk.py","dd_id":"D3","dd_text":"All standalone scripts and the installed package import without unintended side effects"}]},"source_event_uuids":["f71122a2-b618-49ab-a9e8-65ee644ec232","ad5198fd-3a50-4d1c-8621-90ce2f1458c2","bc236d4d-c721-418d-9631-6cd2ccb23563","ca8357fc-78f6-44e8-b22c-ede42b438170","20229636-4401-4408-9f5f-abee1f1e1bac","9696163f-a36a-4379-873a-922031416ec1","dd590a18-5174-4c35-9370-cc929e1d6656","9710f6c9-5a95-450d-adbf-c1746a7fd258","78793b67-bcd4-4019-aca1-e80f514f79f9","cc041d0b-1991-4c04-bdee-5af4f1141a45","ab27fbfc-79e4-48fd-add6-e32596af761e","08aaee31-9396-4215-a182-c7e7e186ea3f","